The application inside app/main.py serves two primary endpoints:

1. Root Endpoint (/) — Welcome & Status Route

Route: GET /

Response:

JSON
{
  "status": "online",
  "message": "DevOps CI/CD Pipeline Active!"
}
Purpose: Acts as the default landing route to verify that the web server is reachable and running.

2. Health Check Endpoint (/health) — DevOps Probe Route

Route: GET /health

Response: HTTP status 200 OK

JSON
{
  "status": "healthy"
}
Purpose: In production systems, cloud platforms, container orchestrators (like Kubernetes), and load balancers continuously ping this endpoint.

If it responds with 200 OK, traffic is sent to the container.

If it fails or stops responding, the platform knows the container crashed or froze and will automatically restart or replace it.

How It Serves Traffic
The server runs on port 5000 (host="0.0.0.0").

Inside the container, Docker exposes this port (EXPOSE 5000) so incoming web requests can reach the Flask server from outside the container.